+
+1. Add failing observable tests using custom AST rules: every listed extension, `.C` vs `.c`, actual PHP tag/mixed HTML/untagged INC, Blade partial state, modern C#, `.h` common/conflicting candidates, original Unicode/encoded spans, duplicate same-line observations, malformed syntax, zero/below/at/above budgets and modified custom semantics. Keep the prior exposed routing draft historical.
+2. Adopt the four exact tested grammar dependencies, preserving existing toolchain and parser runtime. Reconcile actual root lockfile/build dependencies; add language-specific semantic-node selection without enlarging existing seven-language candidate behavior.
+3. Implement ambiguous headers through two bounded candidate parses sharing the current cap allocation. Consolidate identical facts by original occurrence and identity; conflicting interpretation remains partial/unknown. Never infer configured build language, combine conflicting receiver bindings or give each candidate a full independent cap. Preserve custom AST matching and old rule IDs.
